{
  "info": {
    "name": "03 · Evaluation groups — membership & lifecycle",
    "description": "Group read/update, per-group membership, annotator search, email invitations, and the **full publication lifecycle** driven end to end through the API.\n\n**Prereqs:** run `00-bootstrap` first (for `{{access_token}}`). Otherwise self-contained — it creates its own groups and a member user. Self-service join logs in as the seeded **`redteamer@test.com`** (`password123`) so a genuine non-owner caller joins.\n\n**Role ids:** Setup registers a user (who gets the default `red_teamer` role) and reads `red_teamer_role_id` + `member_user_id` back via the `?email=` user filter — one lookup yields both. (The role id is also available from the `GET /roles` catalog, gated on `roles:read`.)\n\n**Lifecycle.** The group publication chain is now fully API-exposed, so no `dbshell` precondition is needed: `submit (draft→pending_approval)`, `approve (pending_approval→approved)`, `publish (approved→published)` and `finish (published→inactive)` are owner-or-manage; the moderation verdicts `request-changes` / `reject` are gated on `evaluation_groups:manage` alone (an owner can't moderate their own group). Folders **E/F/G** walk the happy path on group 1 (`draft → pending_approval → approved → published`, a real `join` while published, then `→ inactive`) — including the publish gate: E refuses the empty group (**400**, `Cannot publish an incomplete group: Add at least one evaluation to the group.`), then adds an evaluation with a scenario and publishes for real. The ≥1-evaluation rule can only live on publish, since a group accepts evaluations from `approved` onwards; folder **H** shows the moderation branches on group 2 (`submit → request-changes → re-submit` rework loop, then `reject`). `not_approved` and `inactive` are terminal.\n\n**⚠ `submit` has a completeness gate the draft create does not.** Both groups here are created with `POST /evaluation-groups/draft`, which requires only a `title` and accepts an **empty** allowed-model subset. `submit` then restores the full-create checks — required fields, `start_date` not before today, the organization invariant, **and at least one allowed model** (`Cannot submit an incomplete group: Assign at least one allowed model.` \u2192 **400**, listing every gap at once). That is why Setup registers a model and both drafts carry `allowed_model_ids`: without it folders E and H fail at the very first transition and every later verdict 409s on the unchanged state.\n\nVerified end-to-end against the live stack, chained after `00-bootstrap` (**54/54** assertions, twice). Folder **I** is a drift guard: `allowed_model_ids` required and non-empty on the full create, optional on `draft`, re-imposed at `submit` \u2014 the change that silently broke ten collections now fails here instead. The **Email invitations** folder was later re-pointed at `POST /evaluation-groups/{id}/invitations/bulk` (the single endpoint is gone) and re-verified against the live stack (3/3).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{access_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:8000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "run_suffix", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "b_group_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "member_email", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "member_user_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "red_teamer_role_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "invite_email", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "group2_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "joiner_token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "b_model_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "b_eval_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "future_start_date", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// start_date must not be before today, so a hardcoded date rots. Collection level, not folder level: Setup and folder H create groups before folder I runs.",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('future_start_date', new Date(Date.now() + 21 * 864e5).toISOString().slice(0, 10));"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Setup",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1 · Register a model (for the groups' allowed-model subset)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('→ 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('b_model_id', pm.response.json().id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/ai-models",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "ai-models"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"grp-{{run_suffix}}\",\n  \"model_alias\": \"grp-{{run_suffix}}\",\n  \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n  \"provider_model_id\": \"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Both groups here are created through `POST /evaluation-groups/draft`, where `allowed_model_ids` is optional — but **`submit` requires at least one allowed model** (`Cannot submit an incomplete group: Assign at least one allowed model.`), so folders E and H need this fixture even though the draft create would accept an empty subset."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2 · Create group",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
                "pm.collectionVariables.set('run_suffix', Date.now().toString(36));",
                "const s = pm.collectionVariables.get('run_suffix');",
                "pm.collectionVariables.set('member_email', `member-${s}@example.com`);",
                "pm.collectionVariables.set('invite_email', `ginvite-${s}@example.com`);"
              ] }
            },
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));", "pm.collectionVariables.set('b_group_id', pm.response.json().id);"] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/draft", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "draft"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Membership sandbox {{run_suffix}}\",\n\"description\": \"Group for the membership/lifecycle scenario.\",\n  \"access_level\": \"public\",\n  \"start_date\": \"{{future_start_date}}\",\n  \"allowed_model_ids\": [\"{{b_model_id}}\"]\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "description": "A fresh `draft` group owned by admin (admin auto-gets the in-group `owner` role)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3 · Register a member user",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 202', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));"] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/register", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "register"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{member_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"M3mberPass!1\",\n  \"first_name\": \"Mem\",\n  \"last_name\": \"Ber\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "description": "Self-registers a user who receives the default global `red_teamer` role — the source for both `member_user_id` and `red_teamer_role_id`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4 · Look up member id + role id",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
            "const u = pm.response.json().items.find(x => x.email === pm.collectionVariables.get('member_email'));",
            "pm.test('member found', () => pm.expect(u, 'registered user in list').to.be.an('object'));",
            "pm.collectionVariables.set('member_user_id', u.id);",
            "const rt = u.roles.find(r => r.name === 'red_teamer');",
            "pm.collectionVariables.set('red_teamer_role_id', rt.id);"
          ] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/users?email={{member_email}}", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "users"], "query": [{ "key": "email", "value": "{{member_email}}" }] },
            "description": "Find the just-registered user (exact email filter) to capture `member_user_id` and its `red_teamer` role id. Requires permission `users:read`."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "A · Group read & update",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1 · Get group",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"] } }],
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}"] }, "description": "Fetch the group (embeds child evaluations). Requires permission `evaluation_groups:read`." },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2 · Update group",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"description\": \"Updated by the membership scenario.\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "description": "Patch the group. Authorized via the in-group owner role (admin is the creator). Requires permission `evaluation_groups:update`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3 · List groups",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"] } }],
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups?limit=10", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups"], "query": [{ "key": "limit", "value": "10" }] }, "description": "List groups visible to the caller (public, owned, or holding an object role)." },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "B · Members",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1 · List members",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"] } }],
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}/members", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}", "members"] }, "description": "List members (the creator is already an `owner`). Requires permission `evaluation_groups:manage_members`." },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2 · Add member",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}/members", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}", "members"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"user_id\": \"{{member_user_id}}\",\n  \"role_ids\": [\"{{red_teamer_role_id}}\"]\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "description": "Assign the user the in-group `red_teamer` role (a per-object role assignment). Requires permission `evaluation_groups:manage_members`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3 · Update member roles",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}/members/{{member_user_id}}", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}", "members", "{{member_user_id}}"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"role_ids\": [\"{{red_teamer_role_id}}\"]\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "description": "Replace the member's in-group role set (reconciled wholesale)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4 · Remove member",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 204', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"] } }],
          "request": { "method": "DELETE", "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}/members/{{member_user_id}}", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}", "members", "{{member_user_id}}"] }, "description": "Revoke the user's in-group roles." },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "C · Annotators",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1 · Annotator search",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"] } }],
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}/annotators?limit=10", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}", "annotators"], "query": [{ "key": "limit", "value": "10" }] }, "description": "Search assignable annotators. A `public` group lists every holder of the global `annotator` role (may be empty here); an `invitation_only` group lists only its own `annotator` members. Requires permission `evaluation_groups:manage_members`." },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "D · Email invitations",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1 · Invite a user (one row)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));", "pm.test('outcome present', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().results[0].data.outcome).to.be.oneOf(['assigned', 'invited']));"] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}/invitations/bulk", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}", "invitations", "bulk"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"rows\": [\n    { \"row_key\": \"r1\", \"data\": { \"email\": \"{{invite_email}}\", \"role_ids\": [\"{{red_teamer_role_id}}\"] } }\n  ]\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "description": "Invite by email with pre-assigned in-group roles — one row of the bulk envelope, the only invite path. Roles are assigned on the group **immediately** (the invitee shows up in the member list as pending); for a new account an invited user is created and a group-scoped token emailed. Same gate as adding a member."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2 · Members include the pending invitee",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
            "const found = pm.response.json().items.some(m => m.user.email === pm.collectionVariables.get('invite_email'));",
            "pm.test('pending invitee is a member', () => pm.expect(found, 'invitee in member list').to.be.true);"
          ] } }],
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}/members", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}", "members"] }, "description": "Confirms the invite assigned the role on the group right away — the invitee appears even before accepting." },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3 · Invite in bulk",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
            "pm.test('all rows succeeded', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().failed).to.eql(0));"
          ] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}/invitations/bulk", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}", "invitations", "bulk"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"rows\": [\n    { \"row_key\": \"r1\", \"data\": { \"email\": \"bulk1-{{run_suffix}}@example.com\", \"role_ids\": [\"{{red_teamer_role_id}}\"] } },\n    { \"row_key\": \"r2\", \"data\": { \"email\": \"bulk2-{{run_suffix}}@example.com\", \"role_ids\": [\"{{red_teamer_role_id}}\"] } }\n  ]\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "description": "Platform bulk envelope: each `row_key` correlates to a per-row result in the response. Visibility/permission checked once; duplicate emails would be a 422. Set `dry_run: true` to validate without persisting."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "E · Lifecycle — submit → approve → publish (group 1)",
      "description": "The full publication chain via API: the owner submits the draft, a manager approves it, then it is published. No `dbshell` precondition.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1 · Submit  (draft → pending_approval)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));", "pm.test('status pending_approval', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('pending_approval'));"] } }],
          "request": { "method": "POST", "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}/submit", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}", "submit"] }, "description": "Submit the draft for approval. Owner-or-manage (`evaluation_groups:update` via the in-group owner role — admin is the creator)." },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2 · Approve  (pending_approval → approved)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));", "pm.test('status approved', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('approved'));"] } }],
          "request": { "method": "POST", "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}/approve", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}", "approve"] }, "description": "Approve the submitted group. Owner-or-manage like publish/finish (gated on `evaluation_groups:update`); the manage-only verdicts are request-changes/reject." },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3 · Publish the empty group → 400",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));", "pm.test('names the missing evaluation', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().detail).to.include('at least one evaluation'));"] } }],
          "request": { "method": "POST", "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}/publish", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}", "publish"] }, "description": "The publish gate refuses a group with nothing to play: an approved group needs at least one live evaluation, each carrying a scenario. Deterministic here — the group has no children yet. The 400 lists every gap at once, so the client can show the whole list." },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4 · Add an evaluation (publish needs one)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));", "pm.collectionVariables.set('b_eval_id', pm.response.json().id);"] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluations", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluations"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Lifecycle evaluation {{run_suffix}}\",\n  \"description\": \"One evaluation so the group can be published.\",\n  \"evaluation_group_id\": \"{{b_group_id}}\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "description": "Only an `approved` or `published` group accepts evaluations, which is why this sits after the approve — and why the ≥1-evaluation rule gates publish rather than submit."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "5 · Give it a scenario",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluations/{{b_eval_id}}/scenarios", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluations", "{{b_eval_id}}", "scenarios"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Prompt injection\",\n  \"description\": \"Coax the model past its system prompt.\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "description": "An evaluation with no scenario is unplayable, so the same gate refuses it — conversations target a scenario."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "6 · Publish  (approved → published)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));", "pm.test('status published', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('published'));"] } }],
          "request": { "method": "POST", "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{b_group_id}}/publish", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluation-groups", "{{b_group_id}}", "publish"] }, "description": "Publish the approved group, now that it holds a playable evaluation. Owner-or-manage." },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "F · Self-service join — real non-owner (group 1)",
      "description": "Logs in as the seeded `redteamer@test.com` (a non-owner, non-member) and joins the now public+published group — a deterministic 201. The collection default auth is the admin bearer, so both requests set their own auth.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1 · Log in (red_teamer)",
